{{also|menacé}}
==English==

===Pronunciation===
* {{IPA|/ˈmɛnɪs/|lang=en}}
* {{rhymes|lang=en|ɛnɪs}}

===Etymology 1===
First attested ''ante'' 1300: from the {{etyl|fro|en}} {{m|fro|manace}}, {{m|fro|menace}}, from the {{etyl|la|en}} {{m|la|minācia}}, from {{m|la|minax||threatening}}, from {{m|la|minor||I threaten}}.

====Noun====
{{en-noun|menaces}}

# a [[perceived]] [[threat]] or [[danger]].
#* Dryden
#*: the dark '''menace''' of the distant war.
# the act of [[threatening]].
# an [[annoying]] and [[bothersome]] person.

